{
  "_readme": [
    "Little Thing of Nowa, ep.02 — why the pet doesn't speak human language.",
    "",
    "The argument: everyone asked why it isn't an AI chatbot → these kids will have AI",
    "agents everywhere by 10 → I want them imaginative instead → they already get",
    "everything too early → Pokemon's animals never speak human and the bond works →",
    "'Pika Pika' is one sound carrying a range of emotion → I Am Groot, three words, any",
    "feeling → so the kid should interpret → and I'm sick of toys bolting on AI lazily →",
    "Miko speaks in its own voice, and the voice changes as the pet grows.",
    "",
    "IP: Pokemon and Guardians of the Galaxy are other people's property. Nothing of",
    "theirs appears on screen — his own spoken words are set as type instead, which is",
    "his speech, not their artwork. Do not source Pikachu or Groot imagery for this.",
    "",
    "Presentation: no card type is used more than three times and none repeats twice in a",
    "row. Full-frame statements/lists/quotes carry the argument's turns; panels carry the",
    "asides; the no-text graphics (cells, annotate) carry the two moments that are better",
    "seen than read. The voice B-roll (speaker fitting, grille macro, audio tests) is",
    "saved for the payoff, where he explains that the pet has its own voice."
  ],
